WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.781
This lab hardware holds single charged atoms

2
00:00:02.781 --> 00:00:05.614
in place, and each atom can act

3
00:00:05.614 --> 00:00:07.262
as a quantum bit.

4
00:00:07.262 --> 00:00:09.095
Here is why that matters.

5
00:00:09.495 --> 00:00:11.492
An ordinary bit is like a switch:

6
00:00:11.492 --> 00:00:13.024
zero or one.

7
00:00:13.024 --> 00:00:14.511
A qubit can be in a blend

8
00:00:14.511 --> 00:00:16.380
of both at once.

9
00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:19.083
Physicists call this superposition.

10
00:00:19.483 --> 00:00:21.735
Qubits can also be entangled,

11
00:00:21.735 --> 00:00:24.336
linked so that measuring one tells you

12
00:00:24.336 --> 00:00:25.694
about the other.

13
00:00:25.694 --> 00:00:28.028
Together, these let some problems be solved

14
00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:29.257
in new ways.

15
00:00:29.657 --> 00:00:31.468
But qubits are fragile.

16
00:00:31.468 --> 00:00:33.082
Heat and noise knock them out of

17
00:00:33.082 --> 00:00:35.717
their state, so today's machines make many

18
00:00:35.717 --> 00:00:38.411
errors, and many must be kept extremely

19
00:00:38.411 --> 00:00:39.338
cold.

20
00:00:39.738 --> 00:00:41.607
They are expected to work alongside ordinary

21
00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:44.127
computers, not replace them,

22
00:00:44.127 --> 00:00:45.717
on problems like new materials,

23
00:00:45.717 --> 00:00:47.946
medicines and security.

24
00:00:47.946 --> 00:00:49.781
They could also break some of today's

25
00:00:49.781 --> 00:00:50.858
encryption.

26
00:00:51.258 --> 00:00:54.207
India approved its National Quantum Mission in

27
00:00:54.207 --> 00:00:57.017
twenty twenty-three, at about six thousand crore

28
00:00:57.017 --> 00:00:59.907
rupees, aiming for computers of fifty to

29
00:00:59.907 --> 00:01:02.611
a thousand qubits within eight years.

30
00:01:03.011 --> 00:01:03.893
For GS Three,

31
00:01:03.893 --> 00:01:05.542
know superposition, entanglement,

32
00:01:05.542 --> 00:01:07.016
and why the world is now building

33
00:01:07.016 --> 00:01:08.791
post-quantum cryptography.

